     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 \u7a00 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nI suspect one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
      }
     ],
